{
  "pedal": "Boss CE-5 Chorus Ensemble — focused reamp, both outputs: the chorus alone on Output A, the dry on Output B",
  "comment": "With a plug in Output B the pedal sends the chorus alone to Output A and the dry to B: the effect by itself, no subtraction. Guitar excerpts (captures/di/) over a steady 8 kHz sine 30 dB under the guitar's peak (the probe: its phase on Output A is the chorus's delay at every moment, guitar or not). Depth 7:00 first (the delay stands still: the chorus's tone, level and clips against the waveform): a sweep, burst ladders at 1 kHz and 200 Hz from -18 to +4 dB (the two clips), chords, funk at -12 dB and full level; then the ladders again with High at 7:00 and with the filters at 12:00 (a clip before a filter keeps its knee, one after it loses it: where the wet clip sits), chords through three filter settings. Then the sweep: each setting's probe alone and guitar over it, at -12 dB and full level, one take twice (the pedal against itself), the lead held out of any fit. Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise; 9:00 and 3:00 pointer horizontal. Low is the Filter's outer ring, High its inner knob. Takes ordered so each step turns one or two knobs.",
